---
// src/components/Faq.astro
---

<section id="faq" class="max-w-4xl xl:max-w-5xl 2xl:max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 sm:py-14 lg:py-18 xl:py-22">
  <div class="text-center mb-8 sm:mb-10 lg:mb-12">
    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 lg:px-4 py-1 lg:py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#EFECE4] border border-[#DDD7CB] text-[#6B655D] text-xs lg:text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2 sm:mb-2.5">
      FAQ
    </div>
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl lg:text-4xl xl:text-5xl font-bold text-[#24211E] tracking-tight">
      Frequently Asked Questions
    </h2>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-3 sm:space-y-4 lg:space-y-5">
    <!-- FAQ 1 -->
    <details class="group rounded-xl lg:rounded-2xl bg-white border border-[#E6E1D6] p-4 sm:p-5 lg:p-6 xl:p-7 transition-all [&_svg]:open:rotate-180">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none text-sm sm:text-base lg:text-lg xl:text-xl font-bold text-[#24211E]">
        <span>How is Unklip completely free with no limits?</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 lg:w-5 lg:h-5 text-[#736B61] transition-transform duration-200 shrink-0 ml-2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
        </svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-3 lg:mt-4 text-xs sm:text-sm lg:text-base xl:text-lg text-[#736B61] leading-relaxed">
        Traditional background removers run on cloud GPU clusters that cost thousands of dollars per month. Unklip uses <strong class="text-[#24211E]">WebGPU</strong> to execute the neural network directly on your computer or phone’s GPU. Because there are no cloud inference costs, we offer full access with zero fees.
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- FAQ 2 -->
    <details class="group rounded-xl lg:rounded-2xl bg-white border border-[#E6E1D6] p-4 sm:p-5 lg:p-6 xl:p-7 transition-all [&_svg]:open:rotate-180">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none text-sm sm:text-base lg:text-lg xl:text-xl font-bold text-[#24211E]">
        <span>Are my images and photos private?</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 lg:w-5 lg:h-5 text-[#736B61] transition-transform duration-200 shrink-0 ml-2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
        </svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-3 lg:mt-4 text-xs sm:text-sm lg:text-base xl:text-lg text-[#736B61] leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-emerald-800">Yes, 100% private.</strong> Your images never leave your browser. They are processed entirely on-device and never saved to any database.
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- FAQ 3 -->
    <details class="group rounded-xl lg:rounded-2xl bg-white border border-[#E6E1D6] p-4 sm:p-5 lg:p-6 xl:p-7 transition-all [&_svg]:open:rotate-180">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none text-sm sm:text-base lg:text-lg xl:text-xl font-bold text-[#24211E]">
        <span>Why does remove.bg charge for high resolution while Unklip doesn’t?</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 lg:w-5 lg:h-5 text-[#736B61] transition-transform duration-200 shrink-0 ml-2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
        </svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-3 lg:mt-4 text-xs sm:text-sm lg:text-base xl:text-lg text-[#736B61] leading-relaxed">
        Remove.bg downsizes free images to 0.25 megapixels as part of their business model to sell credits. Unklip maintains your original resolution and combines the neural alpha matte directly with your native pixels.
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
